      "purpose": "Find the slope of a line of fit and use it to predict.",
      "principles": [
       "PRINCIPLE_MULTIPLE_REPRESENTATIONS"
      ],
      "rationale": "The line of fit is drawn and two points on it are named, so its slope can be found exactly. The student reads the slope as points per hour and uses the line to predict. This is the use of a linear model 8.SP.A.2 and 8.SP.A.3 ask for.",
      "misconceptions": [
       "Predicting from the nearest data point instead of the line.",
       "Reading the slope as the score where the line starts."
      ],
      "references": [
       "Common Core Standards Writing Team (2011), Progressions for the Common Core State Standards in Mathematics, 6–8, Statistics and Probability"
      ]
